---
source: crates/deft-cli/../../tests/unit/help.rs
expression: "help::group(g.name)"
---
deft image - commands (input -> output)
  info         image -> report                  Format, dimensions, EXIF orientation, GPS
  adjust       image -> image                   Change --brightness, --contrast, --saturation, --gamma
  blur         image -> image                   Gaussian blur: --radius 5, or a --box region
  compress     JPEG, PNG or WebP -> image       Smaller file: --quality, --target-size 200KB
  convert      image -> image                   Change format: --to png|jpg|webp|avif|gif|tiff|bmp|ico
  crop         image -> image                   Cut a region: --box x,y,w,h or --aspect 16:9
  favicon      image -> ico+png...              Website icon set: favicon.ico and PNG sizes
  flip         image -> image                   Mirror: --direction horizontal|vertical
  frames       gif -> png...                    Save each frame of an animated GIF as PNG
  grayscale    image -> image                   Remove colour
  meta         image -> image                   Read EXIF, or set --title --author --copyright --date
  montage      image... -> image                Tile images into a grid: --cols 3 --size 300x300
  ocr          image -> txt                     Read the text in an image (tesseract)
  pad          image -> image                   Add a border or canvas: --border 20, --size 1080x1080
  resize       image -> image                   Scale: --size 800x, 1920x1080, 50%
  rotate       image -> image                   Turn clockwise by any angle (EXIF is applied first)
  strip        JPEG, PNG, WebP or GIF -> image  Remove EXIF, GPS and text metadata
  to-gif       image... -> gif                  Animate images into a GIF: --fps 2
  to-pdf       image... -> pdf                  One page per image
  transparent  image -> image                   Make a colour see-through: --color white --fuzz 10
  trim         image -> image                   Cut away plain borders; --speck 4 ignores stray dots
  watermark    image -> image                   Add text or a logo: --text, --image, --position
More: deft image <command> --help
